WEBVTT

00:06.090 --> 00:09.380
<i>In the second quarter
of the 21st century,</i>

00:09.550 --> 00:12.260
<i>the advent of sub-light
transportation</i>

00:12.470 --> 00:15.140
<i>marked the beginning
of an unprecedented wave</i>

00:15.310 --> 00:16.480
<i>of human expansion.</i>

00:29.400 --> 00:33.330
<i>Human explorers discovered
new planetary systems...</i>

00:35.870 --> 00:37.540
<i>and colonized them,</i>

00:39.580 --> 00:42.170
<i>traveling further and further</i>

00:42.460 --> 00:44.550
<i>into the unknown.</i>

00:52.760 --> 00:53.510
What?

01:13.530 --> 01:17.200
<i>In 2057, Earth's
most aggressive neighbors,</i>

01:17.370 --> 01:21.500
<i>the Crogs, launched
a treacherous surprise attack.</i>

01:24.880 --> 01:27.050
<i>Completely caught off guard,</i>

01:27.210 --> 01:31.170
the Earth Coalition
put up a desperate defense.

01:34.140 --> 01:35.800
<i>Their forces held</i>

01:35.970 --> 01:38.810
<i>and the Crogs
were narrowly defeated.</i>

01:39.850 --> 01:43.350
<i>Humans have since lived in peace
with their neighbors.</i>

01:45.940 --> 01:47.320
<i>That is,</i>

01:47.980 --> 01:50.400
<i>until today.</i>

03:25.370 --> 03:27.420
Has she been sitting here all night?

03:27.790 --> 03:28.630
Didn't you hear?

03:28.790 --> 03:31.420
It was her birthday yesterday
and her dad didn't call.

03:31.590 --> 03:32.840
Again.

03:33.050 --> 03:36.130
She has a dad?
I thought she was an orphan.

03:36.380 --> 03:37.300
What's she thinking?

03:37.470 --> 03:39.470
If he's never called,
then he never will.

03:41.430 --> 03:42.600
Hey you!

03:42.810 --> 03:44.430
I'm not deaf, you know?

03:45.600 --> 03:47.940
That's it, just run.
Run away.

03:48.100 --> 03:49.900
I know you're just jealous.

03:50.060 --> 03:54.320
My dad's famous,
the greatest race manager ever!

03:54.990 --> 03:56.490
He's just too...

03:58.030 --> 04:00.410
busy to give me a call.

04:03.790 --> 04:05.410
Not his fault.

04:07.120 --> 04:08.170
Hey, Eva.

04:09.080 --> 04:11.290
There's a package waiting
for you at the front desk.

04:12.000 --> 04:13.090
Look alive.

04:13.250 --> 04:14.210
Yes.

04:15.260 --> 04:16.260
What did I tell you?

04:16.510 --> 04:17.670
I knew it.

04:20.340 --> 04:21.600
Hi, Ned.

04:21.760 --> 04:24.100
I think you have a package
for me from my dad.

04:26.520 --> 04:28.190
Hey, wake up!

04:29.900 --> 04:31.860
I have a package, yes.

04:32.020 --> 04:34.780
Well, I don't think
it's from your dad.

04:37.570 --> 04:41.160
Looks like that part
you ordered months ago.

04:44.080 --> 04:46.240
Don't tell anyone
I let it through.

04:46.410 --> 04:48.000
All right!

04:49.790 --> 04:50.790
You know what, Ned?

04:51.120 --> 04:54.420
If you weren't so old and ugly,
I could kiss you.

04:56.670 --> 04:59.760
If I were 50 years younger.

05:10.020 --> 05:11.440
You are late.

05:16.570 --> 05:17.780
Hello, handsome.

05:17.940 --> 05:19.280
Long time no see.

05:20.740 --> 05:22.780
I've got a little present for you.

05:24.030 --> 05:26.030
Today's going to be a big day.

05:28.290 --> 05:29.580
For you...

05:30.580 --> 05:31.960
and for me.

05:35.840 --> 05:37.000
Eva.

05:37.300 --> 05:40.130
I thought you dismantled
that rocket seat.

05:43.890 --> 05:46.140
Well, don't just stand there.
Stop her!

06:02.820 --> 06:04.660
Yeah!

06:27.350 --> 06:28.930
Early graduation.

07:26.490 --> 07:27.660
<i>Wow.</i>

07:29.370 --> 07:31.080
So this must be the place.

07:36.830 --> 07:37.750
Daddy.

07:46.800 --> 07:48.930
Little girl,
what do you think you're doing?

07:49.090 --> 07:49.930
It's OK.

07:50.180 --> 07:51.390
I'm Don Wei's daughter.

07:51.550 --> 07:52.640
That's a good one.

07:53.310 --> 07:54.890
And believe me,
I've heard everything.

07:55.060 --> 07:56.350
I don't have time to play games.

07:56.520 --> 07:58.940
Now, beat it.
Go on, get out of here.

08:02.860 --> 08:04.730
Don Wei's daughter.

08:29.970 --> 08:31.300
Hey, you!

08:37.310 --> 08:39.140
What are you doing here,
young man?

08:41.020 --> 08:44.020
Do I look like a young man to you?
Can't you see I'm a girl?

08:44.440 --> 08:45.730
Oh, is that so?

08:45.900 --> 08:47.650
Well then, you've got
even less of a reason to be here.

08:47.820 --> 08:49.200
This is not a shopping mall.

08:49.360 --> 08:51.320
You're in the hangar
of a star-racing team.

08:51.490 --> 08:54.330
Now, leave before
I kick you off the premises myself.

08:57.160 --> 08:58.540
This is all a big mistake.

08:59.040 --> 09:00.670
My name's Eva.

09:00.830 --> 09:02.040
I'm your daughter.

09:05.090 --> 09:06.090
You fools.

09:06.250 --> 09:08.340
Didn't I tell you we need this
fixed by tomorrow?

09:08.510 --> 09:10.010
It's the Grand Prix.

09:14.180 --> 09:15.470
Excuse me.
It's the head mechanic.

09:15.640 --> 09:16.560
He can't make it today.

09:16.720 --> 09:18.140
We'll see about that.

09:18.680 --> 09:20.350
Are you crazy?
It's the Grand Prix!

09:21.060 --> 09:22.850
Does that mean anything to you?

09:23.350 --> 09:25.610
You got a day off
last year, didn't you?

09:26.650 --> 09:28.230
What do you mean, twins?

09:29.240 --> 09:30.990
I don't care if they were quintuplets.

09:31.150 --> 09:33.490
I need you here now.
And I mean right now.

09:33.660 --> 09:35.530
I have no replacement for you.

09:35.700 --> 09:37.410
And the primary thruster
is not working.

09:38.200 --> 09:39.620
Much ado
about nothing, really.

09:39.790 --> 09:42.330
-Well, just sell the twins.
-Upgrades never work.

09:42.500 --> 09:44.750
You just need to take off
this piece of junk.

09:44.920 --> 09:46.000
<i>And voilé</i>.

09:46.170 --> 09:47.590
All I care about is the race.

09:51.260 --> 09:53.890
Hey, have you lost
your mind, little girl?

09:57.350 --> 09:59.020
Sir, it's working.

10:01.560 --> 10:02.980
Guess what? You're fired.

10:04.690 --> 10:05.560
Who are you?

10:06.860 --> 10:09.980
<i>We“, uh... I'm... uh...</i>

10:13.780 --> 10:16.030
<i>Um... I'm, uh...</i>

10:16.370 --> 10:18.200
-Spit it out.
-I'm...

10:19.490 --> 10:21.000
We haven't got all day.

10:21.750 --> 10:22.960
I'm...

10:25.790 --> 10:28.630
I'm, <i>um...</i> I'm...

10:34.720 --> 10:36.550
I'm Molly!

10:37.760 --> 10:39.930
Molly, you've got a job.

10:42.310 --> 10:44.980
<i>The hours are from 8:00 am.
to 10:00 p.m., seven days a week,</i>

10:45.150 --> 10:46.690
with a half-hour break for lunch.

10:46.860 --> 10:49.110
Though I would imagine
you won't have time for hunger.

10:50.860 --> 10:54.280
And next time, I suggest
you wear more suitable attire.

10:57.240 --> 11:00.080
Yeah, it was good
to see you, too.

11:03.710 --> 11:05.250
Ah, what now?

11:27.310 --> 11:28.810
I'm looking for Don Wei.

11:29.690 --> 11:31.020
Mr. President?

11:31.480 --> 11:33.070
Wow, serious limo.

11:33.230 --> 11:35.450
I wonder what the president wants
with the boss.

11:35.610 --> 11:36.610
Our new sponsor?

11:36.910 --> 11:38.240
Nah.

11:39.570 --> 11:40.830
Dad?

11:43.160 --> 11:45.660
So what can I do for you?

11:46.710 --> 11:48.920
I'll come straight
to the point, Mr. Wei.

11:49.080 --> 11:50.840
The planet is in need of your help.

11:52.170 --> 11:54.090
I'm afraid I don't follow.

11:54.460 --> 11:57.260
I've been told you're
the best racing manager we've got.

11:57.430 --> 12:00.850
What I'm about to tell you
is top secret.

12:01.140 --> 12:03.720
And must always remain that way.

12:04.390 --> 12:05.560
Oh.

12:06.980 --> 12:07.890
Of course.

12:12.650 --> 12:15.360
<i>It began 25 years ago.</i>

12:15.610 --> 12:17.530
<i>I was just a young councilor then.</i>

12:17.700 --> 12:20.160
<i>The Crogs' final assault
seemed imminent</i>

12:20.320 --> 12:23.280
<i>and we were preparing
for the wurst.</i>

12:23.620 --> 12:24.950
<i>When suddenly...</i>

12:36.170 --> 12:38.760
<i>...this visitor appeared.</i>

12:42.350 --> 12:44.930
Greetings, people of Earth.

12:45.100 --> 12:49.770
Despite your insignificance
in the eyes of the universe,

12:49.940 --> 12:51.980
I, the Avatar,

12:52.150 --> 12:55.860
invite you to join
the beings of the Galaxy

12:56.030 --> 12:59.200
in the Great Race of Oban.

13:00.700 --> 13:02.700
Be ready, the hour

13:03.120 --> 13:06.870
of your ultimate prize is near.

13:20.800 --> 13:22.010
What? A race?

13:22.180 --> 13:24.800
Well, now I've definitely
heard everything.

13:26.970 --> 13:28.430
The Crogs!

13:29.020 --> 13:30.390
Look, they're retreating.

13:30.560 --> 13:31.690
Gentlemen...

13:32.810 --> 13:35.770
No one outside this room
must ever learn

13:35.940 --> 13:37.360
what happened here today.

13:37.530 --> 13:38.940
And I mean no one.

13:39.110 --> 13:41.740
General, what about the race?

13:41.900 --> 13:43.780
What race?
It's ridiculous.

13:43.950 --> 13:45.530
Who would believe us?

13:46.370 --> 13:48.950
Councilor,
consider your career.

13:49.370 --> 13:50.370
<i>Now...</i>

13:51.160 --> 13:52.620
Today we're the heroes

13:52.790 --> 13:55.250
who protected the Earth
from the Crogs.

13:55.710 --> 13:59.300
That's all the public
ever needs to know.

14:06.800 --> 14:09.140
We refused to listen.

14:09.560 --> 14:12.640
But now, the Avatar
has returned.

14:12.940 --> 14:15.230
The truce of the race
of Oban is over,

14:15.400 --> 14:18.270
and the hour
of the ultimate test has come.

14:18.570 --> 14:22.200
We must join the race
or God knows what fate awaits us.

14:22.360 --> 14:23.610
What can I do to help?

14:24.360 --> 14:27.080
The Avatar's vessel leaves at dawn.

14:27.280 --> 14:29.370
Gather the people
you need and go.

14:29.580 --> 14:31.450
We've got 13 hours.

14:31.620 --> 14:33.040
I'll do my best.

14:33.210 --> 14:34.870
YOU can COUflt on me.

14:36.290 --> 14:37.750
<i>And once again,</i>

14:37.920 --> 14:39.920
<i>the champion of the minor leagues...</i>

14:40.590 --> 14:43.090
<i>Rick Thunderbolt!</i>

14:54.480 --> 14:58.440
Congratulations,
champion of the minor leagues.

14:58.610 --> 15:00.270
I knew you could do it, Rick.

15:01.440 --> 15:04.280
Spare me your sarcasm, Don.
You're wasting your time.

15:04.450 --> 15:06.740
I'm never coming back
to your worthless team.

15:07.280 --> 15:09.450
I didn't mention anything
about coming back.

15:16.750 --> 15:17.420
Ready.

15:20.090 --> 15:22.130
Up next, Jordan C. Wilde.

15:22.300 --> 15:24.760
Don, can you tell me exactly
what we're doing here?

15:25.010 --> 15:27.430
I thought we had
a great race to go to.

15:43.530 --> 15:44.860
Where we're going,
you'll be happy

15:45.030 --> 15:46.990
to have a gunner like this one
on board.

15:52.030 --> 15:53.240
<i>Yeah...</i>

15:58.880 --> 16:00.540
He's perfect. We'll take him.

16:03.710 --> 16:05.590
There will be no requisition.

16:05.760 --> 16:07.840
Arrow 1 and 2 are prototypes.

16:08.180 --> 16:10.470
They are not for racing,
do you hear me?

16:10.680 --> 16:12.560
With you,
they'll end up scrap metal.

16:12.720 --> 16:13.600
I won't allow it.

16:13.760 --> 16:15.480
Not in a million years.

16:16.060 --> 16:18.020
Now, get out!

16:20.690 --> 16:24.070
I'll also need
your mechanics, Stan and Koji.

16:25.230 --> 16:27.240
Huh? Impossible!

16:27.400 --> 16:30.740
Stan is my right arm
and Koji is my left.

16:30.910 --> 16:34.080
Precisely. It's a matter
of utmost importance.

16:37.620 --> 16:39.960
Then my arms are your arms.

16:40.460 --> 16:41.130
Yes.

16:42.790 --> 16:43.840
Gentlemen,

16:44.050 --> 16:45.920
take care
of the final preparations.

16:46.130 --> 16:48.970
And assist Stan and Koji
with the engine's revisions.

17:05.230 --> 17:08.650
Now, what are you plotting
behind my back, huh?

17:12.110 --> 17:14.780
If you want out,
this is the moment.

17:15.280 --> 17:16.370
That's fine with us, sir.

17:16.540 --> 17:18.120
We're definitely ready
for the challenge.

17:18.290 --> 17:20.670
You know, for a guppy,
you've got a real big mouth.

17:20.830 --> 17:24.040
Don, tell me at least you've got
a clue as to where we're going?

17:24.340 --> 17:25.460
According to the President,

17:25.630 --> 17:28.800
Oban is located at the epicenter
of the Milky Way.

17:29.510 --> 17:32.260
But first, there are qualifying races
held simultaneously

17:32.430 --> 17:34.930
on three planets
equidistant from Oban.

17:35.300 --> 17:38.390
Here, here, and here.

17:38.890 --> 17:41.690
That's some 25,000
light years away.

17:41.850 --> 17:42.480
<i>Wow.</i>

17:48.150 --> 17:49.440
Oh my.

17:57.870 --> 17:59.700
Don't let them near
the star-racers!

18:05.000 --> 18:06.290
This way, hurry!

18:06.880 --> 18:07.670
What's going on?

18:07.840 --> 18:10.170
It's a Crog.
A Crog's attacking us!

18:10.510 --> 18:11.920
-Rick, get the truck.
-Got it.

18:14.590 --> 18:16.350
-Wait for me.
-Back off.

18:18.560 --> 18:20.220
Let me through!

18:20.730 --> 18:22.480
Wait! Da...!

18:23.020 --> 18:23.770
Let's go.

18:51.170 --> 18:52.340
I'm coming, Dad.

18:59.760 --> 19:01.810
Could this truck be any slower?

19:02.600 --> 19:03.770
Com pa")!-

19:15.910 --> 19:18.410
Fly to the other side
of the Galaxy if you want.

19:18.820 --> 19:20.830
But this time,
I'm coming with you.

19:28.130 --> 19:29.790
Sorry, no Crogs allowed.

19:35.130 --> 19:37.130
Slow down.
I can't get a fix on him.

19:37.340 --> 19:38.010
<i>No.</i>

19:38.680 --> 19:40.100
Rick, hit the brakes.

19:40.300 --> 19:42.140
-What?
-Hit the brakes now!

19:48.350 --> 19:49.060
Yeah!

19:49.230 --> 19:50.980
Faster, we're almost out of time.

19:51.570 --> 19:53.440
Step on it, Rick.

19:55.360 --> 19:57.150
You think you're going to ditch me?

19:58.160 --> 19:59.410
Think again!

20:04.450 --> 20:05.830
The Avatar's ship.

20:06.000 --> 20:07.210
It's almost dawn.

20:07.620 --> 20:09.580
Faster, you piece of junk.

20:15.090 --> 20:16.260
Hang on!

20:28.810 --> 20:31.360
Is this the great race
you were talking about, Don?

20:31.940 --> 20:34.230
Or is it just the warm-up?

20:38.200 --> 20:39.950
Faster, Rick. Faster.

21:10.560 --> 21:11.520
What the?

21:19.900 --> 21:21.740
Hey, this is cool.

21:39.510 --> 21:42.090
The die is cast.

21:43.220 --> 21:45.180
The race has begun.
